<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ahtum</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">early 11th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Ajtony</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ahtum, or Ajtony, was an early 11th-century ruler of the region between the Mureș and the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a>, known from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legend-of-saint-gerard">Legend of Saint Gerard</a>. Baptised in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> rite at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vidin">Vidin</a>, he grew rich by taxing the salt carried on the Mureș and defied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stephen-king-of-england">King Stephen</a> I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>, until the king's commander Csanád defeated and killed him. His lands became the county of Csanád.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ahtum.jpg" alt="Ahtum" width="320" height="187" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: GeorgeBasaraba · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Banatul_Timi%C8%99oarei_.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
